Z||000004||Nashco||04-06-2001||11:28 PM||||I'm going through a hell of a time trying to get the recall work done on my 88.  After several weeks of haggling and a couple inspections, I finally got my dealership to tell me it DIDN'T need done, so I had to call 1800PMCARES and get some bite behind my bark.  They got it authorized for me, and made the recall open on my VIN.  So, after all this, the service manager is trying to tell me my manifold isn't part of the recall, even though it's warped horribly!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  So, I call the NHTSA, as a final resort, only to find that they can only file a complaint, and can't enforce the recall!  What the hell now?  Does anyone know of a dealership in Alabama that works on Fieros, or has a tech and service manager that will at least cooperate?  I have the recall re-opened on my car, just have to find a shop to do it!!!  Ok, I'm done venting now...sort of...wait, still pissed, nevermind <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||04-07-2001||12:24 AM||||Unfortunatly I don't have the text of the V6 fire recall. I don't know what's in that text. See if you can get them or Pontiac/GM to show you the original tect of the recall document sent to dealers. Make sure the dealer is using the document(s) in my cave article. There is more than one recall version for the 4 cyl. this may be true of the V6. The one in my cave is the final version that I know about. It is posible that there are updates I don't know about.<P>At this point you might want to contact your state attourny general.<P>All I know is what NHTSA has put out for public view. Those links are in the recall doc I posted. Read all of them. If NHTSA doesn't comply with published policy then also file a complaint with the U.S. attourny general and/or the GAO. You may not get your car fixed but you can at least make some jacka$s's life uncomfortable.<P>make sure you document everything. The more people who do this the more evidence we gather. the more evidence we gather the more we can make things very hot for GM. We now have over 2000 members. If we can show that GM stonewalls on recalls we have grounds for a class action suite. This could apply to allot more than just our Fiero's. We might not get rich off it but at least we might gat our cars fixed and if we're lucky some cash to give them a paint job or something.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Nashco||04-07-2001||07:34 PM||||I have a link that contains the exact text and pictures of the original recall.  The only difference is it's in a web-friendly format.  My dad worked for Pontiac doing Fiero recalls back in the day, and he's sending me the original recall text, which I'll be scanning and posting on the web.  The recall text is <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/v6recall.htm" TARGET=_blank>here</A>.  This, like I said, is EXACTLY what the dealerships have.  I haved quoted exactly parts of it at the dealership before the Service Manager finally got a copy.  When he did, he felt like a real ass, or at least looked like one, for doubting me.<P>I'm calling the the Alabama Consumer Affairs office of the Attorney General on Monday to file a complaint against the dealership.  Hopefully this will bring a little more attention to this.  I'm hoping if I bring a little attention in from a lot of places, they will give my Fiero what it deserves to avoid any big attention.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
